<section>
<measure n="1" metcon="false"><staff n="1"><layer n="1"><note xml:id="c1_1" dur="4" pname="b" oct="4"><verse n="1"><syl>(repeat)</syl></verse></note><note xml:id="c1_2" dur="4" pname="b" oct="4"><verse n="1"><syl>Sitting</syl></verse></note><note xml:id="c1_3" dur="4" pname="b" oct="4"><verse n="1"><syl>beside</syl></verse></note><note xml:id="c1_4" dur="4" pname="b" oct="4"><verse n="1"><syl>a</syl></verse></note><note xml:id="c1_5" dur="4" pname="b" oct="4"><verse n="1"><syl>well</syl></verse></note></layer></staff><dir staff="1" place="above" startid="#c1_1">1</dir><harm staff="1" place="above" tstamp="1">C</harm><harm staff="1" place="above" tstamp="1">G</harm><harm staff="1" place="above" tstamp="1">F</harm><harm staff="1" place="above" tstamp="1">C</harm></measure>
<measure n="2" metcon="false"><staff n="1"><layer n="1"><note xml:id="c2_1" dur="4" pname="b" oct="4"><verse n="1"><syl>Jesus</syl></verse></note><note xml:id="c2_2" dur="4" pname="b" oct="4"><verse n="1"><syl>saw</syl></verse></note><note xml:id="c2_3" dur="4" pname="b" oct="4"><verse n="1"><syl>her,</syl></verse></note><note xml:id="c2_4" dur="4" pname="b" oct="4"><verse n="1"><syl>a</syl></verse></note><note xml:id="c2_5" dur="4" pname="b" oct="4"><verse n="1"><syl>Samaritan</syl></verse></note></layer></staff></measure>
<measure n="3" metcon="false"><staff n="1"><layer n="1"><note xml:id="c3_1" dur="4" pname="b" oct="4"><verse n="1"><syl>Drawing</syl></verse></note><note xml:id="c3_2" dur="4" pname="b" oct="4"><verse n="1"><syl>near,</syl></verse></note><note xml:id="c3_3" dur="4" pname="b" oct="4"><verse n="1"><syl>seeking</syl></verse></note><note xml:id="c3_4" dur="4" pname="b" oct="4"><verse n="1"><syl>water</syl></verse></note><note xml:id="c3_5" dur="4" pname="b" oct="4"><verse n="1"><syl>there.</syl></verse></note></layer></staff></measure>
</section>
</score></mdiv></body>
<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>How He was moved for her,</l><l>Empty woman—so dissatisfied.</l><l>He spoke a word just to open her.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>“I’ve living water here</l><l>That can fill your deepest longing, dear.</l><l>Ask of Me, I will give it thee.”</l><l> </l><l> Sir, how Your funny words</l><l> Draw me in the heat of day</l><l> I’m not really seeking</l><l> But You started speaking</l><l> And I cannot turn away</l><l> </l><l> Now You mention it, Lord,</l><l> I’m really very hot and dry</l><l> Something tells me</l><l> Out of everything I tried</l><l> That You can satisfy</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Ah, living water, Lord!</l><l>See it running over evermore</l><l>Into my wearied, thirsting heart!</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>Ah, living water, Lord!</l><l>Now a Fountain, gushing evermore</l><l>Out of my full and bursting heart!</l><l> </l><l> How drinking living water</l><l> Does generate a spring!</l><l> Keeps running through me</l><l> Now it’s coming to me</l><l> Why I cannot help but sing!</l><l> </l><l> Then to add to it all</l><l> You tell me it’s forevermore!</l><l> Don’t know how I ever lived before</l><l> But now I want more water Lord!</l></lg>
</div>
</back></music></mei>
